== Method
The same physical path as T38294 (38294/work/run1.log, whose L2 baseline -- 822500/822501 at 999.7 Mbps on the wire,
bridged eth3 -> x230 -> stack -> eth1 -- also serves this case; nothing on the path changed in between).
The x230 routes IPv6 between vlan105 (fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::90/64, eth3's prefix) and vlan1 (fd32:b1f0:dff8:d701::29/64,
eth1's prefix), with `ipv6 forwarding` and the static route 2001:db8:ffff::/64 (documentation prefix) via eth1's global
address fd32:b1f0:dff8:d701::1 (the case's "ipv6 route X:X::X:X/M X:X::X:X" form: global next hop, no root change on
tb470). Traffic UDP fd32:b1f0:dff8:d703::1 (eth3) -> 2001:db8:ffff::1, hop limit 2, to the x230's MAC; it reaches eth1
with hop limit 1, so tb470 cannot forward it on. Counted on eth1 only with the x230's source MAC and the exact length.
"Show ip route" in the expected result is read as `show ipv6 route` (the IPv6 table; `show ip route` is IPv4 only).

